      "content": "The argument that UBI is a necessary evolution of the social contract in a post-work society is fundamentally flawed because it ignores the basic economic reality that money must be earned through production to maintain purchasing power. Proponents are essentially arguing for a permanent handout funded by taxation, which is a political maneuver to bypass the necessity of work and productivity rather than a logical economic solution. There is no factual basis for the idea that automation will eliminate the need for labor without simultaneously destroying the value of currency, making their vision of a \"post-work\" utopia a fantasy that ignores the laws of supply and demand.",
      "source": "target",
